<title>UK: Strike hits Total refinery - official.</title>
<headline>Strike hits Total refinery - official.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 24-hour strike by some workers hit Total SA's 300,000 barrels per day (bpd) Gonfreville refinery on Monday, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The stoppage led to a reduction in the refinery's production, trade sources said.  </p>
<p>The sources said the strike at the Le Havre plant may have also affected output at Total'S 120,000 bpd Dunkirk refinery but this was not confirmed by the spokesman.</p>
<p>&quot;There was industrial action forecast for today. I cannot confirm that there was a reduction in capacity,&quot; the spokesman added.</p>
<p>He said the CGT union had said that 60 percent of the workforce was affected by the strike but he had no information on Dunkirk.</p>
<p>The sources said they expected the strike to finish on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
